@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{slack-extras.el} extends the @samp{emacs-slack} package with personal workflow integrations that depend on external packages not bundled with @samp{emacs-slack}. The package provides:

@itemize
@item
Extended org link storage that adds @code{slack-activity-feed-buffer-mode} support to @samp{ol-emacs-slack} (@ref{Link storage}).
@item
Commands to capture the message at point to personal or work inboxes (@ref{Capture}).
@item
Local ActivityWatch channel context for selected channel and thread buffers (@ref{ActivityWatch context}).
@item
A tab-bar notification element showing Slack unreads and mentions (@ref{Tab-bar notifications}).
@item
Team registration with session credentials read from Chrome (@ref{Credentials from Chrome}).
@end itemize

The package depends on @samp{slack} and @samp{ol}.

@node Link storage
@chapter Link storage

@findex slack-extras--store-link
The function @code{slack-extras--store-link} replaces @code{ol/slack-store-link} as the @samp{emacs-slack} link `:store` handler via @code{org-link-set-parameters}. It delegates to the original @code{ol/slack-store-link} in @code{slack-message-buffer-mode} and @code{slack-thread-message-buffer-mode}, and adds support for @code{slack-activity-feed-buffer-mode} by reading the @code{ts} and @code{room-id} text properties at point. This makes @code{org-store-link} and capture templates that use @code{%a} work in the activity feed.

